  "goodToKnow": "Predigen means to preach: in der Kirche predigen. Figuratively, it means to lecture people: Hör auf zu predigen! Die Predigt is a sermon, and der Prediger the preacher. Wasser predigen und Wein trinken means to preach water and drink wine, to be a hypocrite; it goes back to Heinrich Heine's poem Deutschland. Ein Wintermärchen (1844). Luther, the most famous German Prediger, translated the Bible into German."
